  "description": "About JsonFucker\n\nI’m a student from Taiwan, and to be honest, my English isn't great, so I’m using AI to help introduce JsonFucker.\n\nI created this package out of sheer frustration with standard solutions like JsonSerializer and raw JsonElement handling—they just felt clunky and inconvenient for my workflow.\n\nCore Features & Design:\n\nSimplified Parsing Logic: Under the hood, it maps JSON directly into a Dictionary<string, JsonElement>. Without getting too bogged down in low-level details, this approach drastically speeds up JSON parsing and makes property extraction far more intuitive.\n\nStreamlined API Integration: I combined JSON serialization directly with HttpClient, allowing developers to attach JSON payloads to API HTTP requests seamlessly with minimal boilerplate.",
